# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-8, 2.1-20). L §5.7 What a kind can be: "The parts clauses (tally 2.1, §3.6) are body lines
# of a place kind: owned by D [ties by e], batched, step u and takes k for w ..., in that order. A kind that states
# owned by or batched states step and takes, and step or takes stands only beside one of them. Its sign rule is min 0,
# and it is no subkind of assets ... D is a def of type num keyed by an event kind and by parties (either a subkind), in
# that order, at the law date m.day of its movement key m. A subkind of a kind that keeps parts keeps its clauses and
# states none of its own; a subkind of a place kind that keeps none may state them for its own things. Anything else is
# refused (LOAD-PARTS)." L §8.3 LOAD-PARTS's messages.
# L §3.6: "owns[p, x] at such a place is refused (LOAD-PARTS): one place has one source of ownership"; L §8.3
# `owns[<p>, <x>]: <x> keeps parts`.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
input owns[p in parties, x in places]: num
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  owns[ania, konto] = 1
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARTS owns[ania, konto]: konto keeps parts ...
